<Shell title="Aero · Blind Validation Challenge 01" description="Input freeze, sealed experimental references and an isolated model review. No production prediction or experimental comparison has occurred." path="/software/aero/evidence/benchmarks/blind-validation-01/">
<header><p class="eyebrow">EXTERNAL BENCHMARK / CHALLENGE 01</p><span class="status pending">INPUT FROZEN · RESULT NOT EVALUATED</span><h1>Freeze the prediction before revealing the answer.</h1><p>The experimental series is selected and its answers are sealed. An isolated model review is complete. <strong>Solver criteria are not frozen; no production CFD run or prediction exists yet.</strong></p><div class="links"><a class="primary" href={input+'input.json'}>Inspect permitted inputs →</a><a href="#blockers">Current hold points ↓</a></div></header>
<section aria-labelledby="chronology"><h2 id="chronology">Actual chronology</h2><ol class="timeline">{state.phases.map((p,i)=><li><strong>{i+1}. {p.label}</strong><span>{p.status==='FROZEN'?'FROZEN':'NOT OCCURRED'}</span></li>)}</ol><p class="subtle">Input freeze preserves stated facts and unknowns. It is not preregistration or permission to solve.</p></section>
<section><h2>One complete experimental series.</h2><p><strong>NASA TM-4074, Table XIII, first subtable.</strong> NACA 0012 at Mach 0.15, chord Reynolds number 5.95 million, with localized No. 180 grit strips at x/c = 0.05 on both surfaces.</p><p>All 18 operating points are retained, from −3.99° to 19.27°, including both near-zero points. The comparison will cover 36 CL/CD observations. No difficult angles have been trimmed. This is a polar distribution, not a spatial Cp field.</p><div class="links"><a href="https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/19880019495">NASA source record ↗</a><a href={input+'custody.json'}>Custody and transcription review</a><a href={original+'selection.json'}>Original candidate-selection record</a></div><details><summary>Source, rights and remaining uncertainty</summary><p>The 97-page source was archived and hashed. The selected table was checked against its page image and printed lift/drag ratios. NASA metadata permits government public use; the eventual reveal will contain attributed numerical observations, not a republished scan.</p><p>Measured coordinates, trailing-edge convention, series temperature, trip height and inlet turbulence are not invented. The tunnel turbulence level was explicitly unknown. These uncertainties need a declared numerical treatment before production.</p></details></section>
<section class="boundary"><h2>Reference withholding—not total prior ignorance.</h2><p>The source custodian has seen the answers and is not the predictor. Source selection itself was not blind. A fresh Gemma 3 12B reviewer received only the input document, without inherited conversation, source PDF, reference values, key, browsing or RAG.</p><p>The review ran in a disposable, non-root, network-disabled container. Its only mounted data were read-only model weights; its home was temporary. The desktop RTX 3090 performed inference. Model pretraining familiarity with this canonical benchmark cannot be excluded.</p></section>
<section><div class="cards"><article><h2>What Aero may know</h2><p>The <a href={input+'input.json'}>input JSON</a>: geometry description, operating points, test conditions, facility methods and explicit unknowns. No expected coefficients or successful CFD choices.</p></article><article><h2>What stays sealed</h2><p>36 measured lift/drag values in AES-256-GCM ciphertext. The source, plaintext extraction and key stay outside the repository and all predictor mounts.</p><div class="links"><a href={input+'reference.enc'}>Sealed ciphertext ↓</a><a href={input+'reference-metadata.json'}>Reference commitments</a></div></article></div></section>
<section><h2>Input-only model review: HOLD.</h2><p>The model identified missing geometry, fluid-property, transition and tunnel-treatment decisions. Its suggestion that steady-state treatment should suffice across the series is <strong>not accepted as established</strong>. The high-angle conditions require an explicit time-treatment decision.</p><p>Unavailable measured coordinates need not make a declared nominal-geometry approximation impossible. The review is retained for audit; it does not become engineering authority.</p><div class="links"><a href={base+'fresh-review.raw.txt'}>Unedited model response</a><a href={base+'input-only-prompt.txt'}>Complete input-only prompt</a><a href={base+'fresh-review.json'}>Actual inference isolation receipt</a></div></section>
<section><h2>Solver isolation passed. Numerical readiness is open.</h2><p>A separate non-root OpenFOAM container passed a filesystem/network probe and started the solver help command. Its only mounts were a read-only input file and fresh output directory. Root writes and external TCP access were rejected; no Docker socket, corpus, source or reference was exposed.</p><p>This is a readiness probe, <strong>not a mesh or CFD solve</strong>. An audited production driver, three-grid strategy and complete frozen criteria remain required.</p><div class="links"><a href={base+'solver-isolation.json'}>Enforced container configuration</a><a href={base+'solver-probe.log'}>Probe output</a></div></section>
<section><h2>Preregistered acceptance criteria</h2><span class="status pending">NOT FROZEN</span><p>No numerical or experimental acceptance threshold has been frozen. The next specification must address transition equivalence, unknown turbulence, corrected free-air comparison, geometry approximation and unsteady behavior across all registered points.</p><a href={original+'preregistration.draft.json'}>Original incomplete draft →</a><details><summary>Comparison rules already implemented</summary><p>Per-quantity absolute RMSE and maximum absolute error; exact station matching and full-series coverage. Unknown uncertainty cannot widen bounds after unseal. Failed numerical adequacy prevents an overall scientific PASS. PASS, FAIL and MIXED are all preserved.</p></details></section>
<section><h2>Scientific commitments</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Stage</th><th>SHA-256 / chronology</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Input package</td><td><code>{state.scientific_hashes.input_package}</code></td></tr><tr><td>Sealed reference</td><td><code>{state.scientific_hashes.sealed_reference}</code></td></tr><tr><td>Input timestamp</td><td><a href={input+'state.json'}>Frozen event record</a> · <a href="https://github.com/alexthegreat714/alex-blythe-site/commits/main/public/demos/aero/blind-validation-01-input-v1/input.json">Publication commit history ↗</a></td></tr><tr><td>Criteria / prediction / comparison</td><td>Not frozen / not occurred</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Git records are auditable history, not a trusted timestamp service or immutability against administrators. No predictor is permitted the decryption key before an anchored prediction.</p></section>
<section id="blockers"><h2>What still needs to happen</h2><ol>{state.blockers.map(item=><li>{item}</li>)}</ol><p>Then solve, freeze and publish the complete prediction, reveal the reference and compare automatically. Failed or difficult outcomes must remain visible.</p></section>
<section id="downloads"><h2>Inspect this checkpoint</h2><p>19 software tests pass. The checkpoint contains frozen inputs, encrypted reference, actual isolation receipts and the input-only review. There is no experimental result or production saved case.</p><div class="links"><a class="primary" href={base+'checkpoint-sources.zip'}>Checkpoint source package ↓</a><a href={base+'README.md'}>Checkpoint explanation</a><a href={base+'status.json'}>Current status JSON</a><a href={base+'manifest.json'}>Checkpoint hashes</a><a href={input+'manifest.json'}>Input hashes</a></div><details><summary>Preserved original preparation release</summary><p>Preparation 0.1 documents the earlier framework-only state and is unchanged. It is not the current experiment status.</p><div class="links"><a href={original+'protocol-paper.pdf'}>Original LaTeX protocol PDF ↗</a><a href={original+'preparation-sources.zip'}>Original source package ↓</a><a href={original+'manifest.json'}>Original hashes</a></div></details></section>
<section class="boundary"><h2>No external-validation claim yet.</h2><p>This checkpoint demonstrates source custody and isolated readiness work. It does not establish numerical adequacy, experimental agreement or design readiness. The scientific result remains NOT EVALUATED.</p></section>
